1348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Does my child need Biomimetic Dentistry?)
/E (Does my child need Biomimetic Dentistry?)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This is the one exception. Baby teeth, or primary teeth, do not need biomimetic dentistry. Baby teeth will fall out, unlike the adult teeth that you need to keep for 80+ years. Traditional dental fillings and dental crowns are adequate place holders for baby teeth.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Biomimetic dentistry takes much more time and is much more technique sensitive, which is not conducive to doing dental work on children. For example, biomimetic dentistry requires a rubber dam and a completely dry environment, which Is near Impossible with a wiggly child.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (If you have young kids, your priority should be making sure your child does not experience dental trauma, and that Is less likely to occur If the dentist can finish treatment in a short amount of time. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In chapter 8, we go Into dental trauma In more depth, but If It occurs during childhood, research shows that they are more likely to experience poor oral health going forward Into adulthood.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Parents also ask me if they should put their child under general anesthesia for their dental work as recommended by their pediatric dentist. This Is a very personal decision that you need to make based on your comfort level. However, please keep In mind that electing this may help prevent dental trauma, which is crucial to a lifetime of good oral health. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3471 0 R
/E ( Pending your child has deep cavities, dental crowns are okay on baby teeth and can survive longer than large fillings. Pulpotomies are always done with pediatric dental crowns.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3472 0 R
/E ( The most Important thing Is to find a dentist that your child trusts so that they do not experience any dental trauma as a child. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
