1591 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The goal of airway medicine is to get a person breathing through their nose day and night. The tongue is the on-off switch for nasal breathing! When your tongue rests on the roof of the mouth, it signals to your body to breathe through the nose. When your tongue rests on the floor of the mouth, your body is more likely to default to mouth breathing. This is particularly the case at night because you lose awareness of tongue posture and whether your lips are closed or not. )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [10 11 12]
>>
endobj
