/T (Orthodontist)
/E (Orthodontist)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1622 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (For older kids ages 7-12, expansion via a Rapid Palate Expander is a great option to create more space for the tongue and teeth. Most orthodontists want to wait until age seven when the permanent molars have erupted, so they can attach the expander to the molars. But I think we would see amazing results if orthodontists were willing to place expanders at a younger age. The palate fuses around age 12, so after that age, expansion is minimal. An expander can still be used after the palate fuses but the gains in width will be from tipping the teeth outwards, not from physical expansion of the jaw. More aggressive expansion of a fused palate without surgery is unstable, unpredictable, and unnecessary.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
