1628 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Tongue mobility refers to the flexibility and the range of motion of the tongue. Ideally, the tongue can comfortably reach the roof of the mouth without compensation. Compensation is when the floor of the mouth lifts up in order for the tongue to reach the roof of the mouth. You can test this by placing your index finger under your tongue on the floor of your mouth and then try lifting the tongue up. Can you get much mobility?)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
