1635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (An airway obstruction refers to any obstruction in the nose or the mouth that prevents you from breathing properly. This includes conditions such as chronic congestion or variations in anatomy such as a deviated septum, small nasal passage, or enlarged tonsils and adenoids. All of these restrict the size of the airway in one area or another and, therefore restrict the flow of air into and out of the lungs. There is only so much space available!)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
