<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Flexible Spending Accounts \(FSA\) and Health Savings Accounts \(HSA\): These are tax-advantaged savings accounts that allow you to set aside money pre-tax to pay for qualified medical expenses. HSAs are available to self-employed individuals, but FSAs are not. The individual employee owns the HSA and can carry it to different employers, while a health FSA is not portable and is associated with the employer. You can use FSA or HSA funds to pay for dental expenses with pre-tax dollars, reducing the overall cost.)
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
