2574 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Abscess - A tooth abscess is an area of infection around the root of a dead infected tooth typically contained within the bone. In rare cases, the tooth abscess can spread to other areas of the face and cause serious health complications. The abscess can occur in different areas near the tooth for various reasons. A periodontal abscess occurs deep within the pocket of the gum tissue. This can spread deep towards the root of the tooth and dissolve the bone around the neighboring tooth.)
/Pg 101 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2575 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Adenoids - Adenoids are lymphoid tissue high up in the throat where the nasal passage ends and the throat begins and above where the tonsils are located. Like tonsils, adenoids help keep the body healthy by trapping harmful bacteria and viruses that we breathe in.)
/Pg 101 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2576 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 829 0 R
/Pg 101 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
