/T (Coblation Tonsillectomy -  This is an alternative technique to a tonsillectomy performed with a scalpel or with electrocautery \(the worst\), where surgeons can precisely remove part of the tonsil tissue by dissolving the tonsils at the molecular level. This allows for the surgeon to, if the tissue is healthy enough, leave a portion of the tonsil tissue to serve its intended function. Coblation tonsillectomy has significantly lower intraoperative bleeding, takes less time than a traditional tonsillectomy, and has less postoperative pain.)
/E (Coblation Tonsillectomy -  This is an alternative technique to a tonsillectomy performed with a scalpel or with electrocautery \(the worst\), where surgeons can precisely remove part of the tonsil tissue by dissolving the tonsils at the molecular level. This allows for the surgeon to, if the tissue is healthy enough, leave a portion of the tonsil tissue to serve its intended function. Coblation tonsillectomy has significantly lower intraoperative bleeding, takes less time than a traditional tonsillectomy, and has less postoperative pain.)
