/T (Tooth Death Cycle - is a cycle set in motion when you get a cavity. It explains how traditional dental restorations break down over time, leading to more and more dental work. Biomimetic dentistry is designed to stop the cycle in its tracks, meaning it repairs the tooth in a way that prevents you from continuing to go down this cycle, which costs you thousands over your lifetime. Equally important is getting to the root cause of why you are getting cavities. See chapter 3.)
